{
  "lines": [
    "Meditation",
    "Through silent exposition",
    "revealed",
    "the Supreme Brahman principle",
    "the youth",
    "At the end of their advanced years",
    "sitting",
    "by the group of sages",
    "surrounded",
    "by those established in Brahman",
    "The supreme among teachers",
    "holding in hand",
    "the Chinmudra and the embodiment of bliss",
    "Rejoicing in His own Self",
    "with a joyful face",
    "I praise Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "The universe",
    "like a city seen in a mirror",
    "existing within oneself",
    "Seeing within the Self",
    "by Maya (illusion)",
    "as if manifested outside",
    "like",
    "in sleep",
    "Who",
    "directly realizes",
    "at the time of awakening",
    "His own non-dual Self",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Like a sprout inside a seed",
    "this universe",
    "previously undifferentiated",
    "again",
    "by the imagination of space and time created by Maya",
    "painted with variety",
    "Like a magician",
    "unfolds",
    "like a great yogi",
    "who",
    "by His own free will",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Whose alone",
    "radiance",
    "though the true reality, appears as false",
    "appears",
    "Through the direct declaration 'That Thou Art'",
    "by the words of the Vedas",
    "who",
    "enlightens those who take refuge",
    "By whose direct realization there is no",
    "return into the ocean of worldly existence",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Like the radiance of a great lamp placed inside a pot with many holes",
    "shining",
    "Knowledge",
    "whose",
    "indeed",
    "through the senses like the eyes",
    "outwards",
    "vibrates (manifests)",
    "'I know', thus",
    "Him alone",
    "shining, this entire follows in shining",
    "universe",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "The body",
    "the vital breath and senses",
    "the moving",
    "intellect",
    "and",
    "the void",
    "they consider",
    "Like women, children, the blind, and the ignorant, saying 'I'",
    "deluded",
    "excessively",
    "argue",
    "The destroyer of the great delusion created by the play of Maya's power",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Like the sun and moon eclipsed by Rahu",
    "due to the covering of Maya",
    "Pure existence",
    "due to the withdrawal of the senses",
    "who slept deeply",
    "the man",
    "Saying 'I slept before'",
    "at the time of awakening",
    "who",
    "remembers",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Even in childhood and other stages",
    "in waking and other states",
    "and likewise",
    "in all conditions as well",
    "Following through the changing states as the inner 'I'",
    "shining",
    "always",
    "His own Self",
    "reveals",
    "to the devotees",
    "who",
    "by the auspicious gesture",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "The universe",
    "sees",
    "as cause and effect",
    "from the relation of master and servant",
    "As disciple and teacher",
    "and similarly",
    "as father, son, etc.",
    "through differences",
    "In dream",
    "in waking",
    "or",
    "who",
    "this",
    "man (soul)",
    "is deluded by Maya",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "Earth, water, fire, air, space, the sun",
    "the moon",
    "the soul",
    "Thus appears",
    "this animate and inanimate",
    "whose alone",
    "eightfold form",
    "Nothing else",
    "whatsoever",
    "exists",
    "for those who reflect",
    "beyond whom, the Supreme Lord",
    "To Him",
    "to the divine Guru form",
    "salutations",
    "this",
    "to Lord Dakshinamurthy",
    "That all is the Self",
    "has been made clear",
    "because in this",
    "hymn",
    "Therefore by its",
    "listening, reflecting on its meaning, and meditating",
    "and singing",
    "Along with the great glory of the all-pervading Self",
    "lordship occurs",
    "spontaneously",
    "It is attained, and again the eightfold",
    "manifested",
    "unobstructed divine power",
    "Thus",
    "composed by Shri Adi Shankaracharya",
    "Dakshinamurthy Stotram",
    "is complete"
  ]
}